    <item>
      <title>Texas Political Shift Portends a Shift in US Corporate Power</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-09/texas-political-shift-portends-a-shift-in-us-corporate-power</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7806dc14eb6160a16e665927</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:30:18 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>In 2023, the Republican-majority Texas legislature created a new set of regional courts to handle complex commercial disputes, and a new statewide 15th Court of Appeals to hear cases from those courts (as well as any lawsuits against the state). Texas has been trying to persuade more businesses to incorporate there, and dedicated business courts are seen as a lure because the judges presumably know what they’re doing and are less likely to deliver weird decisions than generalist local courts.</description>
      <dc:creator>Justin Fox</dc:creator>
